  Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL
  was not distributed with this file, You can obtain one
  at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Adam.Elf.Writer.adam - a SectionSet as an ELF64 relocatable object (DESIGN
  sec 7, PLAN-LINUX64 LX2a)

  Every layout fact is the System V gABI's (ELF header, section header,
  symbol table, relocation entries, section groups, extended section
  numbering) with elf.h's names and values (std System.Elf); the relocation
  types are the x86_64 psABI's.

  ElfMachine      what ELF records of an arch: e_machine, the relocation type
                  each RelocKind becomes, the opcodes whose 32-bit operand is
                  a call's or a jump's target (that field is a PLT32, as an
                  assembler writes `call f`), and the page size an image's
                  segments align to and the byte its code gaps are filled
                  with (ElfMachineX86_64); for reading a
                  foreign object (Adam.Elf.Foreign, LX3a) the types that mean
                  nothing, the 32-bit pc-relative ones (S + A - P) and the
                  GOT-relative ones (a slot holding S, its address + A - P);
                  for a dynamic exe (Adam.Elf.Linker, LX3b) the psABI's
                  interpreter, the slot relocation the loader fills
                  (GLOB_DAT), Adam's own _start (glibc crt1.o's: the
                  kernel's argc / argv and the loader's fini to the C
                  runtime's start routine, its main's address and the call
                  through the routine's slot at the fields named) and a
                  routine's stub (a jump through its slot: the target of a
                  foreign call to a shared library's routine); for a C
                  object's thread-locals in an exe (Adam.Elf.Foreign, LX3d2)
                  the psABI's TLS relaxations to local-exec (GNU ld's): the
                  general-dynamic sequence (the bytes before and after its
                  TLSGD field, then the call of TlsGetAddr whose pc-relative
                  field ends it) and its local-exec bytes with their TPOFF32
                  field, the local-dynamic one (TLSLD) and its bytes (no
                  field), and the initial-exec loads (GOTTPOFF: a REX prefix,
                  an opcode and a rip-relative ModRM before the field; each
                  prefix / opcode's local-exec one, the ModRM's register
                  moved into a register-direct ModRM: an immediate)
  WriteElfObject  the object (ET_REL), laid out in this order: the ELF
                  header, then the contents in section index order (each at
                  its alignment), then the section header table.
                  Deterministic: every list in the SectionSet's id order.

  Section indices: 0 the null section; then one SHT_GROUP (GRP_COMDAT) per
  Shared section (a generic instance's code: COMDAT ANY), its members that
  section, every section going with it (Associate) and their .rela
  sections, its signature the first symbol defined in it (the gABI puts a
  group ahead of its members); then the SectionSet's sections in id order,
  each named by its group name (an ELF object may hold many sections of one
  name: a function's piece is one of many .text sections), a Tombstone
  one's with ADAM_ELF_TOMBSTONE_SUFFIX (as COFF's: Adam's linker reads it
  back; GNU's linkers fold the dotted name into its group); then a
  .rela<name> per section with relocations; then .symtab, .symtab_shndx
  (only past SHN_LORESERVE sections: extended numbering, e_shnum 0 and the
  count in section 0's sh_size, e_shstrndx SHN_XINDEX and the index in its
  sh_link), .strtab, .shstrtab. A section going with another that is not
  Shared (an unwind piece, SU2.7's Associate) is SHF_LINK_ORDER with sh_link
  its partner, so a linker's garbage collection drops it with it.

  Kinds: Code .text-like (AX), ReadOnly (A), Data (WA), Zeroed (WA,
  SHT_NOBITS), ThreadLocal (WAT), Info (SHF_EXCLUDE: never in an image, as
  COFF's LNK_REMOVE; H4); a section in the group ADAM_ELF_SECTION_INIT_ARRAY
  is SHT_INIT_ARRAY (WA). A Debug section has no ELF form yet (DWARF is a
  later plan) and raises.

  Symbols: the null symbol, then the internal (STB_LOCAL) Defined symbols,
  then the others (STB_GLOBAL) in id order: a Defined one at its section and
  offset (STT_FUNC in a code section, STT_TLS in a thread-local one, else
  STT_OBJECT, STT_NOTYPE in an Info one), an Undefined one in SHN_UNDEF
  (STT_TLS when a SecRel32 names it, as an ELF linker checks); then one
  undefined symbol per import name no SectionSet symbol has (an ELF object
  names an imported routine by its own name: the linker makes its PLT / GOT
  slot; a program's routine of that name binds the slot instead, as COFF's
  local import does). A relocation (RELA: the addend in the record, the
  field left zero) is:
    Rel32     S + A - (P + 4): R_X86_64_PC32 with A - 4, or R_X86_64_PLT32
              in code after a call / jump opcode; of an Import (the code
              reads the routine's address from its slot) R_X86_64_GOTPCREL
              with A - 4, the slot being the GOT's
    Rva32     R_X86_64_PC32 with A: ELF has no 32-bit image-relative
              relocation, so on ELF the field holds its target relative to
              the field itself (S + A - P: position independent, any ELF
              linker, a .so too); the linux unwinder reads field + value
    Abs64     R_X86_64_64 with A
    SecRel32  a thread-local's offset in its image's TLS block:
              R_X86_64_DTPOFF32 with A
    TpOff32   a thread-local's offset from the thread pointer (local-exec):
              R_X86_64_TPOFF32 with A
    Section   no ELF form (debug information only): raises

  Every fact the object cannot hold (a Debug section, an empty name or one
  with a zero byte, a relocation field that is not zero, a SecRel32 / TpOff32
  not naming a thread-local, a Section relocation, an Abs64 of an Import, an
  Undefined symbol no name finds (an unplaced slot: a link's, never an
  object's), a Shared section that defines no symbol) is a compiler bug and
  raises, naming it.
*******************************************************************************/

module unit Adam.Elf.Writer;

import System.SysUtils, Adam.Core.Common, Adam.Core.Containers, Adam.Backend.Sections, System.Elf;

public const
  // Raised (see the header)
  ADAM_ELF_FAULT_NO_INPUT: string = "ELF writer: no sections or no machine";
  ADAM_ELF_FAULT_DEBUG: string = "ELF writer: a debug section has no ELF form yet: ";
  ADAM_ELF_FAULT_NAME: string = "ELF writer: a name that is empty or holds a zero byte: ";
  ADAM_ELF_FAULT_FIELD: string = "ELF writer: a relocation field that is not zero: ";
  ADAM_ELF_FAULT_RELOC: string = "ELF writer: a relocation ELF cannot write: ";
  ADAM_ELF_FAULT_SLOT: string = "ELF writer: an undefined symbol no name finds: ";
  ADAM_ELF_FAULT_SIGNATURE: string = "ELF writer: a shared section that defines no symbol: ";
  // The C start list section (StartListPlace.Entry on ELF): SHT_INIT_ARRAY, what the
  // loader and glibc's start run
  ADAM_ELF_SECTION_INIT_ARRAY: string = ".init_array";
  // What a Tombstone section's name ends with (see the header)
  ADAM_ELF_TOMBSTONE_SUFFIX: string = ".adam_tombstone";
  // The record sizes of ELF64 (the gABI's Elf64_Ehdr, Elf64_Shdr, Elf64_Sym, Elf64_Rela)
  ADAM_ELF_HEADER_SIZE: int64 = 64;
  ADAM_ELF_SECTION_HEADER_SIZE: int64 = 64;
  ADAM_ELF_SYMBOL_SIZE: int64 = 24;
  ADAM_ELF_RELA_SIZE: int64 = 24;
  // A section group's and an SHT_SYMTAB_SHNDX's word
  ADAM_ELF_WORD_SIZE: int64 = 4;
  // The alignment of the 8-byte tables (relocations, symbols, the section headers)
  ADAM_ELF_TABLE_ALIGN: int64 = 8;
  // The x86_64 page, the opcodes whose rel32 is a call's (E8) or a jump's (E9) target
  ADAM_ELF_PAGE_X86_64: int64 = 4096;
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_CALL: uint8 = 0xE8;
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_JUMP: uint8 = 0xE9;
  // x86_64's int3, an image's code gap fill
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_INT3: int64 = 0xCC;
  // x86_64's dynamic exe pieces (see the header; GNU as's bytes): the psABI's interpreter;
  // _start = endbr64; xor ebp, ebp; mov r9, rdx; pop rsi; mov rdx, rsp; and rsp, -16;
  // push rax; push rsp; xor r8d, r8d; xor ecx, ecx; lea rdi, [rip + main];
  // call [rip + slot]; hlt; a stub = jmp [rip + slot], int3 to 8 bytes
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_INTERPRETER: string = "/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64" + ADAM_EXT_ELF_SO + ".2";
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_START: array[0..37] of uint8 = [
    0xF3, 0x0F, 0x1E, 0xFA, 0x31, 0xED, 0x49, 0x89, 0xD1, 0x5E, 0x48, 0x89, 0xE2,
    0x48, 0x83, 0xE4, 0xF0, 0x50, 0x54, 0x45, 0x31, 0xC0, 0x31, 0xC9,
    0x48, 0x8D, 0x3D, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0xFF, 0x15, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0xF4];
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_START_MAIN_AT: int64 = 27;
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_START_CALL_AT: int64 = 33;
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_STUB: array[0..7] of uint8 = [0xFF, 0x25, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0xCC, 0xCC];
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_STUB_SLOT_AT: int64 = 2;
  // x86_64's TLS relaxations to local-exec (the psABI's / GNU ld's byte forms, see the
  // header): general-dynamic = data16 lea rdi, [rip + x@tlsgd]; data16 data16 rex64 call
  // __tls_get_addr@plt -> mov rax, fs:[0]; lea rax, [rax + x@tpoff]; local-dynamic =
  // lea rdi, [rip + x@tlsld]; call __tls_get_addr@plt -> data16 x3 mov rax, fs:[0];
  // initial-exec = mov / add r64, [rip + x@gottpoff] -> mov / add r64, x@tpoff
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLS_GET_ADDR: string = "__tls_get_addr";
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_BEFORE: array[0..3] of uint8 = [0x66, 0x48, 0x8D, 0x3D];
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_AFTER: array[0..3] of uint8 = [0x66, 0x66, 0x48, 0xE8];
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_LE: array[0..15] of uint8 = [0x64, 0x48, 0x8B, 0x04, 0x25, 0, 0, 0, 0,
    0x48, 0x8D, 0x80, 0, 0, 0, 0];
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_LE_AT: int64 = 12;
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSLD_BEFORE: array[0..2] of uint8 = [0x48, 0x8D, 0x3D];
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSLD_AFTER: array[0..0] of uint8 = [0xE8];
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSLD_LE: array[0..11] of uint8 = [0x66, 0x66, 0x66, 0x64, 0x48, 0x8B, 0x04,
    0x25, 0, 0, 0, 0];
  // initial-exec: REX.W / REX.WR -> REX.W / REX.WB, mov r64, r/m64 -> mov r/m64, imm32, add
  // r64, r/m64 -> add r/m64, imm32; ModRM mod 00 r/m 101 (rip) -> mod 11, reg 000, r/m reg
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_REX: array[0..1] of uint8 = [0x48, 0x4C];
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_REX_LE: array[0..1] of uint8 = [0x48, 0x49];
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_OPS: array[0..1] of uint8 = [0x8B, 0x03];
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_OPS_LE: array[0..1] of uint8 = [0xC7, 0x81];
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_MODRM_RIP_MASK: int64 = 0xC7;
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_MODRM_RIP: int64 = 0x05;
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_MODRM_DIRECT: int64 = 0xC0;
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_MODRM_REG_SHIFT: int64 = 3;
  ADAM_ELF_X86_64_MODRM_REG_MASK: int64 = 7;

const
  // The writer's own section names
  ADAM_ELF_RELA_PREFIX: string = ".rela";
  ADAM_ELF_SECTION_GROUP: string = ".group";
  ADAM_ELF_SECTION_SYMTAB: string = ".symtab";
  ADAM_ELF_SECTION_SHNDX: string = ".symtab_shndx";
  ADAM_ELF_SECTION_STRTAB: string = ".strtab";
  ADAM_ELF_SECTION_SHSTRTAB: string = ".shstrtab";

public type
  // What ELF records of an arch (see the header)
  ElfMachine = object
    Machine: int64;
    RelocPc32: int64;
    RelocPlt32: int64;
    RelocAbs64: int64;
    RelocGotPcRel: int64;
    RelocDtpOff32: int64;
    // A thread-local's offset from the thread pointer (TpOff32: local-exec)
    RelocTpOff32: int64;
    // The opcodes a call's or a jump's 32-bit target field follows
    CallOpcodes: ByteArray;
    // A foreign object's relocation types (see the header): none, 32-bit pc-relative,
    // GOT-relative 32-bit
    RelocNone: int64;
    PcRelTypes: Int64Array;
    GotRelTypes: Int64Array;
    // The arch's page: an image's segment alignment (the ELF linker, LX3)
    PageSize: int64;
    // The byte an image's code gaps are filled with (x86_64's int3)
    CodeFill: int64;
    // A dynamic exe's (see the header): the interpreter, the slot relocation, _start's
    // bytes and its main / call fields, a stub's bytes and its slot field (each field a
    // 32-bit pc-relative one ending its instruction)
    Interpreter: string;
    RelocGlobDat: int64;
    StartCode: ByteArray;
    StartMainAt: int64;
    StartCallAt: int64;
    StubCode: ByteArray;
    StubSlotAt: int64;
    // A C object's TLS relaxations to local-exec (see the header): the types, the call's
    // routine, the general-dynamic bytes around its field and its local-exec bytes (the
    // TPOFF32 field at TlsGdLeAt), the local-dynamic ones, the initial-exec prefixes and
    // opcodes (each one's local-exec at the same index) and the ModRM's rip form (Mask /
    // Rip), its direct form (Direct | the register: (ModRM shr Shift) & RegMask)
    RelocTlsGd: int64;
    RelocTlsLd: int64;
    RelocGotTpOff: int64;
    TlsGetAddr: string;
    TlsGdBefore: ByteArray;
    TlsGdAfter: ByteArray;
    TlsGdLe: ByteArray;
    TlsGdLeAt: int64;
    TlsLdBefore: ByteArray;
    TlsLdAfter: ByteArray;
    TlsLdLe: ByteArray;
    GotTpOffRex: ByteArray;
    GotTpOffRexLe: ByteArray;
    GotTpOffOps: ByteArray;
    GotTpOffOpsLe: ByteArray;
    ModRmRipMask: int64;
    ModRmRip: int64;
    ModRmDirect: int64;
    ModRmRegShift: int64;
    ModRmRegMask: int64;

    init(const AMachine: int64; const ARelocPc32: int64; const ARelocPlt32: int64;
      const ARelocAbs64: int64; const ARelocGotPcRel: int64; const ARelocDtpOff32: int64;
      const APageSize: int64);
    begin
      self.Machine := AMachine;
      self.RelocPc32 := ARelocPc32;
      self.RelocPlt32 := ARelocPlt32;
      self.RelocAbs64 := ARelocAbs64;
      self.RelocGotPcRel := ARelocGotPcRel;
      self.RelocDtpOff32 := ARelocDtpOff32;
      self.RelocTpOff32 := 0;
      self.PageSize := APageSize;
      setlength(self.CallOpcodes, 0);
      self.RelocNone := 0;
      self.CodeFill := 0;
      setlength(self.PcRelTypes, 0);
      setlength(self.GotRelTypes, 0);
      self.Interpreter := "";
      self.RelocGlobDat := 0;
      setlength(self.StartCode, 0);
      self.StartMainAt := 0;
      self.StartCallAt := 0;
      setlength(self.StubCode, 0);
      self.StubSlotAt := 0;
      self.RelocTlsGd := -1;
      self.RelocTlsLd := -1;
      self.RelocGotTpOff := -1;
      self.TlsGetAddr := "";
      setlength(self.TlsGdBefore, 0);
      setlength(self.TlsGdAfter, 0);
      setlength(self.TlsGdLe, 0);
      self.TlsGdLeAt := 0;
      setlength(self.TlsLdBefore, 0);
      setlength(self.TlsLdAfter, 0);
      setlength(self.TlsLdLe, 0);
      setlength(self.GotTpOffRex, 0);
      setlength(self.GotTpOffRexLe, 0);
      setlength(self.GotTpOffOps, 0);
      setlength(self.GotTpOffOpsLe, 0);
      self.ModRmRipMask := 0;
      self.ModRmRip := 0;
      self.ModRmDirect := 0;
      self.ModRmRegShift := 0;
      self.ModRmRegMask := 0;
    end;

    // True when ATypes holds AType
    const method HoldsType(const ATypes: Int64Array; const AType: int64): bool;
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to len(ATypes) - 1 do
        if ATypes[LI] = AType then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;

    // True when the 32-bit field at AOffset of the code section ASection is a call's or a
    // jump's target (the byte before it one of CallOpcodes)
    const method IsCallField(const ASection: ref Section; const AOffset: int64): bool;
    var
      LByte: uint8;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      if (ASection.Kind <> SectionKind.Code) or (AOffset < 1) then
        return false;
      end;
      LByte := ASection.Bytes[AOffset - 1];
      for LI := 0 to len(self.CallOpcodes) - 1 do
        if self.CallOpcodes[LI] = LByte then
          return true;
        end;
      end;
      return false;
    end;
  end;

// x86_64's ElfMachine (the psABI's relocation types, E8 call / E9 jmp rel32; a foreign
// object's PC32 / PLT32 pc-relative, GOTPCREL / GOTPCRELX / REX_GOTPCRELX through a slot; a
// dynamic exe's interpreter, GLOB_DAT, _start and stub; the TLS relaxations)
public routine ElfMachineX86_64(): ref ElfMachine;
var
  LMachine: ref ElfMachine;
  LI: int64;
begin
  LMachine := ref ElfMachine(EM_X86_64, R_X86_64_PC32, R_X86_64_PLT32, R_X86_64_64,
    R_X86_64_GOTPCREL, R_X86_64_DTPOFF32, ADAM_ELF_PAGE_X86_64);
  setlength(LMachine.CallOpcodes, 2);
  LMachine.CallOpcodes[0] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_CALL;
  LMachine.CallOpcodes[1] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_JUMP;
  LMachine.RelocNone := int64(R_X86_64_NONE);
  LMachine.RelocTpOff32 := int64(R_X86_64_TPOFF32);
  LMachine.CodeFill := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_INT3;
  setlength(LMachine.PcRelTypes, 2);
  LMachine.PcRelTypes[0] := int64(R_X86_64_PC32);
  LMachine.PcRelTypes[1] := int64(R_X86_64_PLT32);
  setlength(LMachine.GotRelTypes, 3);
  LMachine.GotRelTypes[0] := int64(R_X86_64_GOTPCREL);
  LMachine.GotRelTypes[1] := int64(R_X86_64_GOTPCRELX);
  LMachine.GotRelTypes[2] := int64(R_X86_64_REX_GOTPCRELX);
  LMachine.Interpreter := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_INTERPRETER;
  LMachine.RelocGlobDat := int64(R_X86_64_GLOB_DAT);
  setlength(LMachine.StartCode, len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_START));
  for LI := 0 to len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_START) - 1 do
    LMachine.StartCode[LI] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_START[LI];
  end;
  LMachine.StartMainAt := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_START_MAIN_AT;
  LMachine.StartCallAt := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_START_CALL_AT;
  setlength(LMachine.StubCode, len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_STUB));
  for LI := 0 to len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_STUB) - 1 do
    LMachine.StubCode[LI] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_STUB[LI];
  end;
  LMachine.StubSlotAt := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_STUB_SLOT_AT;
  LMachine.RelocTlsGd := int64(R_X86_64_TLSGD);
  LMachine.RelocTlsLd := int64(R_X86_64_TLSLD);
  LMachine.RelocGotTpOff := int64(R_X86_64_GOTTPOFF);
  LMachine.TlsGetAddr := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLS_GET_ADDR;
  setlength(LMachine.TlsGdBefore, len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_BEFORE));
  for LI := 0 to len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_BEFORE) - 1 do
    LMachine.TlsGdBefore[LI] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_BEFORE[LI];
  end;
  setlength(LMachine.TlsGdAfter, len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_AFTER));
  for LI := 0 to len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_AFTER) - 1 do
    LMachine.TlsGdAfter[LI] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_AFTER[LI];
  end;
  setlength(LMachine.TlsGdLe, len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_LE));
  for LI := 0 to len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_LE) - 1 do
    LMachine.TlsGdLe[LI] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_LE[LI];
  end;
  LMachine.TlsGdLeAt := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSGD_LE_AT;
  setlength(LMachine.TlsLdBefore, len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSLD_BEFORE));
  for LI := 0 to len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSLD_BEFORE) - 1 do
    LMachine.TlsLdBefore[LI] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSLD_BEFORE[LI];
  end;
  setlength(LMachine.TlsLdAfter, len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSLD_AFTER));
  for LI := 0 to len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSLD_AFTER) - 1 do
    LMachine.TlsLdAfter[LI] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSLD_AFTER[LI];
  end;
  setlength(LMachine.TlsLdLe, len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSLD_LE));
  for LI := 0 to len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSLD_LE) - 1 do
    LMachine.TlsLdLe[LI] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_TLSLD_LE[LI];
  end;
  setlength(LMachine.GotTpOffRex, len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_REX));
  setlength(LMachine.GotTpOffRexLe, len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_REX));
  for LI := 0 to len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_REX) - 1 do
    LMachine.GotTpOffRex[LI] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_REX[LI];
    LMachine.GotTpOffRexLe[LI] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_REX_LE[LI];
  end;
  setlength(LMachine.GotTpOffOps, len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_OPS));
  setlength(LMachine.GotTpOffOpsLe, len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_OPS));
  for LI := 0 to len(ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_OPS) - 1 do
    LMachine.GotTpOffOps[LI] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_OPS[LI];
    LMachine.GotTpOffOpsLe[LI] := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_GOTTPOFF_OPS_LE[LI];
  end;
  LMachine.ModRmRipMask := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_MODRM_RIP_MASK;
  LMachine.ModRmRip := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_MODRM_RIP;
  LMachine.ModRmDirect := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_MODRM_DIRECT;
  LMachine.ModRmRegShift := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_MODRM_REG_SHIFT;
  LMachine.ModRmRegMask := ADAM_ELF_X86_64_MODRM_REG_MASK;
  return LMachine;
end;

// Raises unless AName has bytes and none of them is zero
routine DoCheckName(const AName: string);
var
  LI: int64;
begin
  if len(AName) = 0 then
    raise(ADAM_ELF_FAULT_NAME + "empty");
  end;
  for LI := 0 to len(AName) - 1 do
    if uint8(AName[LI]) = 0 then
      raise(ADAM_ELF_FAULT_NAME + IntToStr(LI) + " in a name of " + IntToStr(len(AName)) +
        " bytes");
    end;
  end;
end;

// The SHF_* flags of a section of AKind (see the header)
routine DoKindFlags(const AKind: SectionKind): uint64;
begin
  match AKind of
    SectionKind.Code: return SHF_ALLOC | SHF_EXECINSTR;
    SectionKind.ReadOnly: return SHF_ALLOC;
    SectionKind.Data: return SHF_ALLOC | SHF_WRITE;
    SectionKind.Zeroed: return SHF_ALLOC | SHF_WRITE;
    SectionKind.ThreadLocal: return SHF_ALLOC | SHF_WRITE | SHF_TLS;
    SectionKind.Info: return SHF_EXCLUDE;
    SectionKind.Debug: return 0;
  end;
  return 0;
end;

type
  // One section header as the writer lays it out, in index order
  ElfHeaderEntry = record
    NameAt: int64;
    HeaderType: uint32;
    Flags: uint64;
    FileAt: int64;
    ByteSize: int64;
    Link: int64;
    Info: int64;
    Align: int64;
    EntrySize: int64;
  end;

  // One symbol table entry: its name's offset in .strtab, st_info, its section's index
  // (0 undefined) and its value
  ElfSymbolEntry = record
    NameAt: int64;
    SymbolInfo: uint8;
    SectionIndex: int64;
    SymbolValue: int64;
  end;

  // A string table being built: the bytes after the leading zero, each name once
  ElfStrings = object
    hidden FText: string;
    hidden FOffsets: ref StringIdMap;

    init();
    begin
      // offset 0 is the empty name: one zero byte
      self.FText := "";
      setlength(self.FText, 1);
      self.FText[0] := char(0);
      self.FOffsets := ref StringIdMap(0);
    end;

    // AName's offset in the table, added (NUL-ended) the first time
    method OffsetOf(const AName: string): int64;
    var
      LOffset: int64;
    begin
      if len(AName) = 0 then
        return 0;
      end;
      LOffset := self.FOffsets.Find(AName);
      if LOffset <> 0 then
        return LOffset;
      end;
      LOffset := len(self.FText);
      self.FText := self.FText + AName;
      setlength(self.FText, len(self.FText) + 1);
      self.FText[len(self.FText) - 1] := char(0);
      self.FOffsets.Put(AName, LOffset);
      return LOffset;
    end;

    property Text: string read FText;
  end;

  // One object's writing (see the header)
  ElfWriter = object
    hidden FSet: ref SectionSet;
    hidden FMachine: ref ElfMachine;
    hidden FBytes: ByteArray;
    // Per section id: its index, its .rela's index (0: none), the index of the group it is
    // a member of (0: none; a Shared section's own), the next member of its group (the
    // chain starts at the Shared section, 0 ends it) and the last one (a Shared section's)
    hidden FSectionIndex: Int64Array;
    hidden FRelaIndex: Int64Array;
    hidden FGroupIndex: Int64Array;
    hidden FGroupShared: Int64Array;
    hidden FNextMember: Int64Array;
    hidden FLastMember: Int64Array;
    // Per symbol id: its symbol table index; true when a SecRel32 names it (STT_TLS)
    hidden FSymbolIndex: Int64Array;
    hidden FThreadSymbol: BoolArray;
    // An import's name -> its symbol table index, when no SectionSet symbol has it
    hidden FImportNames: ref StringIdMap;
    hidden FSymbols: array of ElfSymbolEntry;
    hidden FSymbolCount: int64;
    hidden FFirstGlobal: int64;
    hidden FHeaders: array of ElfHeaderEntry;
    hidden FHeaderCount: int64;
    hidden FSymtabIndex: int64;
    hidden FShndxIndex: int64;
    hidden FStrtabIndex: int64;
    hidden FShstrtabIndex: int64;
    hidden FStrings: ref ElfStrings;
    hidden FSectionNames: ref ElfStrings;
    hidden FHeadersAt: int64;

    init(const ASet: ref SectionSet; const AMachine: ref ElfMachine);
    var
      LI: int64;
    begin
      self.FSet := ASet;
      self.FMachine := AMachine;
      setlength(self.FSectionIndex, ASet.SectionCount);
      setlength(self.FRelaIndex, ASet.SectionCount);
      setlength(self.FGroupIndex, ASet.SectionCount);
      setlength(self.FGroupShared, ASet.SectionCount);
      setlength(self.FNextMember, ASet.SectionCount);
      setlength(self.FLastMember, ASet.SectionCount);
      for LI := 0 to ASet.SectionCount - 1 do
        self.FSectionIndex[LI] := 0;
        self.FRelaIndex[LI] := 0;
        self.FGroupIndex[LI] := 0;
        self.FGroupShared[LI] := 0;
        self.FNextMember[LI] := 0;
        self.FLastMember[LI] := 0;
      end;
      setlength(self.FSymbolIndex, ASet.SymbolCount);
      setlength(self.FThreadSymbol, ASet.SymbolCount);
      for LI := 0 to ASet.SymbolCount - 1 do
        self.FSymbolIndex[LI] := 0;
        self.FThreadSymbol[LI] := false;
      end;
      self.FImportNames := ref StringIdMap(0);
      self.FSymbolCount := 0;
      self.FFirstGlobal := 0;
      self.FHeaderCount := 0;
      self.FSymtabIndex := 0;
      self.FShndxIndex := 0;
      self.FStrtabIndex := 0;
      self.FShstrtabIndex := 0;
      self.FStrings := ref ElfStrings();
      self.FSectionNames := ref ElfStrings();
      self.FHeadersAt := 0;
    end;

    // AValue's low ACount bytes at AAt, least significant first
    hidden method DoPut(const AAt: int64; const AValue: uint64; const ACount: int64);
    begin
      PutLe(self.FBytes, AAt, AValue, ACount);
    end;

    // The name section AId has in the object: its group name, a Tombstone section's with
    // ADAM_ELF_TOMBSTONE_SUFFIX (see the header)
    hidden const method DoObjectName(const AId: int64): string;
    var
      LSection: ref Section;
    begin
      LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(AId);
      if LSection.Tombstone then
        return LSection.GroupName + ADAM_ELF_TOMBSTONE_SUFFIX;
      end;
      return LSection.GroupName;
    end;

    // Raises for what ELF cannot hold of the sections (see the header)
    hidden const method DoCheckSections();
    var
      LId: int64;
      LSection: ref Section;
    begin
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
        if LSection.Kind = SectionKind.Debug then
          raise(ADAM_ELF_FAULT_DEBUG + LSection.SectionName);
        end;
        DoCheckName(self.DoObjectName(LId));
      end;
    end;

    // Every section's index (see the header), the groups' member chains, the tables'
    // indices; the null section is index 0
    hidden method DoNumberSections();
    var
      LId: int64;
      LNext: int64;
      LShared: int64;
      LSection: ref Section;
    begin
      LNext := 1;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        if self.FSet.SectionAt(LId).Shared then
          self.FGroupIndex[LId] := LNext;
          self.FGroupShared[LId] := LId;
          self.FLastMember[LId] := LId;
          LNext := LNext + 1;
        end;
      end;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        self.FSectionIndex[LId] := LNext;
        LNext := LNext + 1;
        // a section going with a Shared one joins its group, after the members before it
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
        if (not LSection.Shared) and (LSection.Associate <> 0) and
          self.FSet.SectionAt(LSection.Associate).Shared then
          LShared := LSection.Associate;
          self.FGroupIndex[LId] := self.FGroupIndex[LShared];
          self.FGroupShared[LId] := LShared;
          self.FNextMember[self.FLastMember[LShared]] := LId;
          self.FLastMember[LShared] := LId;
        end;
      end;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        if self.FSet.SectionAt(LId).RelocCount > 0 then
          self.FRelaIndex[LId] := LNext;
          LNext := LNext + 1;
        end;
      end;
      self.FSymtabIndex := LNext;
      LNext := LNext + 1;
      // extended numbering once the count (with .strtab and .shstrtab) reaches the reserve
      if LNext + 2 > int64(SHN_LORESERVE) then
        self.FShndxIndex := LNext;
        LNext := LNext + 1;
      end;
      self.FStrtabIndex := LNext;
      self.FShstrtabIndex := LNext + 1;
      self.FHeaderCount := LNext + 2;
      setlength(self.FHeaders, self.FHeaderCount);
    end;

    // Marks every symbol a SecRel32 / TpOff32 names (STT_TLS); raises for one that is no
    // thread-local
    hidden method DoMarkThreadSymbols();
    var
      LId: int64;
      LR: int64;
      LSection: ref Section;
      LReloc: ref SectionReloc;
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
    begin
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
        for LR := 0 to LSection.RelocCount - 1 do
          LReloc := LSection.RelocAt(LR);
          if (LReloc.Kind <> RelocKind.SecRel32) and (LReloc.Kind <> RelocKind.TpOff32) then
            skip;
          end;
          LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(LReloc.Symbol);
          if (LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Import) or ((LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Defined) and
            (self.FSet.SectionAt(LSymbol.SectionId).Kind <> SectionKind.ThreadLocal)) then
            raise(ADAM_ELF_FAULT_RELOC + "a " + RelocKindText(LReloc.Kind) + " of " +
              LSymbol.SymbolName + ", no thread-local, in " + LSection.SectionName);
          end;
          self.FThreadSymbol[LReloc.Symbol] := true;
        end;
      end;
    end;

    // A symbol table entry: its index
    hidden method DoAddSymbol(const AName: string; const ABind: uint8; const AType: uint8;
      const ASectionIndex: int64; const AValue: int64): int64;
    var
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      if self.FSymbolCount >= len(self.FSymbols) then
        setlength(self.FSymbols, self.FSymbolCount * 2 + 16);
      end;
      LIndex := self.FSymbolCount;
      self.FSymbols[LIndex].NameAt := self.FStrings.OffsetOf(AName);
      self.FSymbols[LIndex].SymbolInfo := uint8((ABind shl 4) | AType);
      self.FSymbols[LIndex].SectionIndex := ASectionIndex;
      self.FSymbols[LIndex].SymbolValue := AValue;
      self.FSymbolCount := LIndex + 1;
      return LIndex;
    end;

    // Symbol AId's entry (see the header) with binding ABind
    hidden method DoAddSetSymbol(const AId: int64; const ABind: uint8);
    var
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
      LType: uint8;
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(AId);
      DoCheckName(LSymbol.SymbolName);
      if LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Defined then
        match self.FSet.SectionAt(LSymbol.SectionId).Kind of
          SectionKind.Code: LType := STT_FUNC;
          SectionKind.ThreadLocal: LType := STT_TLS;
          SectionKind.Info: LType := STT_NOTYPE;
        else
          LType := STT_OBJECT;
        end;
        LIndex := self.FSectionIndex[LSymbol.SectionId];
        self.FSymbolIndex[AId] := self.DoAddSymbol(LSymbol.SymbolName, ABind, LType, LIndex,
          LSymbol.Offset);
        return;
      end;
      // an Undefined symbol is found by its name (a placed slot no name finds is a link's)
      if self.FSet.FindSymbol(LSymbol.SymbolName) <> AId then
        raise(ADAM_ELF_FAULT_SLOT + LSymbol.SymbolName);
      end;
      LType := STT_NOTYPE;
      if self.FThreadSymbol[AId] then
        LType := STT_TLS;
      end;
      self.FSymbolIndex[AId] := self.DoAddSymbol(LSymbol.SymbolName, ABind, LType, 0, 0);
    end;

    // The symbol table (see the header): locals, then globals, then the import names
    hidden method DoNumberSymbols();
    var
      LId: int64;
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
      LName: string;
      LKnown: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
    begin
      // the null symbol
      self.DoAddSymbol("", STB_LOCAL, STT_NOTYPE, 0, 0);
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SymbolCount - 1 do
        LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(LId);
        if (LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Defined) and LSymbol.Internal then
          self.DoAddSetSymbol(LId, STB_LOCAL);
        end;
      end;
      self.FFirstGlobal := self.FSymbolCount;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SymbolCount - 1 do
        LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(LId);
        if (LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Undefined) or
          ((LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Defined) and not LSymbol.Internal) then
          self.DoAddSetSymbol(LId, STB_GLOBAL);
        end;
      end;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SymbolCount - 1 do
        LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(LId);
        if LSymbol.Kind <> SymbolKind.Import then
          skip;
        end;
        LName := self.FSet.ImportAt(LSymbol.ImportId).ImportName;
        DoCheckName(LName);
        // a symbol of the import's name (a program's routine of a C name) is the slot's
        LKnown := self.FSet.FindSymbol(LName);
        if (LKnown <> 0) and (self.FSet.SymbolAt(LKnown).Kind <> SymbolKind.Import) then
          self.FSymbolIndex[LId] := self.FSymbolIndex[LKnown];
          skip;
        end;
        LIndex := self.FImportNames.Find(LName);
        if LIndex = 0 then
          LIndex := self.DoAddSymbol(LName, STB_GLOBAL, STT_NOTYPE, 0, 0);
          self.FImportNames.Put(LName, LIndex);
        end;
        self.FSymbolIndex[LId] := LIndex;
      end;
    end;

    // The symbol table index of the first symbol defined in the Shared section AId (its
    // group's signature); raises when none is
    hidden const method DoSignatureOf(const AId: int64): int64;
    var
      LS: int64;
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
    begin
      for LS := 1 to self.FSet.SymbolCount - 1 do
        LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(LS);
        if (LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Defined) and (LSymbol.SectionId = AId) then
          return self.FSymbolIndex[LS];
        end;
      end;
      raise(ADAM_ELF_FAULT_SIGNATURE + self.FSet.SectionAt(AId).SectionName);
    end;

    // The members a group's word list names: the Shared section AId's chain, then their
    // .rela sections, in chain order
    hidden const method DoGroupWords(const AId: int64): Int64Array;
    var
      LWords: Int64Array;
      LCount: int64;
      LMember: int64;
    begin
      setlength(LWords, 0);
      LCount := 0;
      LMember := AId;
      while LMember <> 0 do
        setlength(LWords, LCount + 1);
        LWords[LCount] := self.FSectionIndex[LMember];
        LCount := LCount + 1;
        LMember := self.FNextMember[LMember];
      end;
      LMember := AId;
      while LMember <> 0 do
        if self.FRelaIndex[LMember] <> 0 then
          setlength(LWords, LCount + 1);
          LWords[LCount] := self.FRelaIndex[LMember];
          LCount := LCount + 1;
        end;
        LMember := self.FNextMember[LMember];
      end;
      return LWords;
    end;

    // The header entry at AIndex
    hidden method DoHeader(const AIndex: int64; const AName: string; const AType: uint32;
      const AFlags: uint64; const ASize: int64; const ALink: int64; const AInfo: int64;
      const AAlign: int64; const AEntrySize: int64);
    begin
      self.FHeaders[AIndex].NameAt := self.FSectionNames.OffsetOf(AName);
      self.FHeaders[AIndex].HeaderType := AType;
      self.FHeaders[AIndex].Flags := AFlags;
      self.FHeaders[AIndex].FileAt := 0;
      self.FHeaders[AIndex].ByteSize := ASize;
      self.FHeaders[AIndex].Link := ALink;
      self.FHeaders[AIndex].Info := AInfo;
      self.FHeaders[AIndex].Align := AAlign;
      self.FHeaders[AIndex].EntrySize := AEntrySize;
    end;

    // Every section header entry (see the header), file places still to be laid
    hidden method DoDescribeSections();
    var
      LId: int64;
      LSection: ref Section;
      LType: uint32;
      LFlags: uint64;
      LLink: int64;
      LGroupFlag: uint64;
    begin
      self.DoHeader(0, "", SHT_NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0);
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
        if LSection.Shared then
          self.DoHeader(self.FGroupIndex[LId], ADAM_ELF_SECTION_GROUP, SHT_GROUP, 0,
            ADAM_ELF_WORD_SIZE * (1 + len(self.DoGroupWords(LId))), self.FSymtabIndex,
            self.DoSignatureOf(LId), ADAM_ELF_WORD_SIZE, ADAM_ELF_WORD_SIZE);
        end;
      end;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(LId);
        LType := SHT_PROGBITS;
        LFlags := DoKindFlags(LSection.Kind);
        if LSection.Kind = SectionKind.Zeroed then
          LType := SHT_NOBITS;
        end;
        if LSection.GroupName = ADAM_ELF_SECTION_INIT_ARRAY then
          LType := SHT_INIT_ARRAY;
          LFlags := SHF_ALLOC | SHF_WRITE;
        end;
        LGroupFlag := 0;
        if self.FGroupIndex[LId] <> 0 then
          LGroupFlag := SHF_GROUP;
        end;
        LLink := 0;
        if (self.FGroupIndex[LId] = 0) and (LSection.Associate <> 0) then
          LFlags := LFlags | SHF_LINK_ORDER;
          LLink := self.FSectionIndex[LSection.Associate];
        end;
        self.DoHeader(self.FSectionIndex[LId], self.DoObjectName(LId), LType, LFlags | LGroupFlag,
          LSection.Size(), LLink, 0, LSection.Align, 0);
        if self.FRelaIndex[LId] <> 0 then
          self.DoHeader(self.FRelaIndex[LId], ADAM_ELF_RELA_PREFIX + self.DoObjectName(LId), SHT_RELA,
            SHF_INFO_LINK | LGroupFlag, ADAM_ELF_RELA_SIZE * LSection.RelocCount, self.FSymtabIndex,
            self.FSectionIndex[LId], ADAM_ELF_TABLE_ALIGN, ADAM_ELF_RELA_SIZE);
        end;
      end;
      self.DoHeader(self.FSymtabIndex, ADAM_ELF_SECTION_SYMTAB, SHT_SYMTAB, 0,
        ADAM_ELF_SYMBOL_SIZE * self.FSymbolCount, self.FStrtabIndex, self.FFirstGlobal,
        ADAM_ELF_TABLE_ALIGN, ADAM_ELF_SYMBOL_SIZE);
      if self.FShndxIndex <> 0 then
        self.DoHeader(self.FShndxIndex, ADAM_ELF_SECTION_SHNDX, SHT_SYMTAB_SHNDX, 0,
          ADAM_ELF_WORD_SIZE * self.FSymbolCount, self.FSymtabIndex, 0, ADAM_ELF_WORD_SIZE,
          ADAM_ELF_WORD_SIZE);
      end;
      self.DoHeader(self.FStrtabIndex, ADAM_ELF_SECTION_STRTAB, SHT_STRTAB, 0,
        len(self.FStrings.Text), 0, 0, 1, 0);
      // .shstrtab names itself: its size once every name, its own included, is in
      self.DoHeader(self.FShstrtabIndex, ADAM_ELF_SECTION_SHSTRTAB, SHT_STRTAB, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0);
      self.FHeaders[self.FShstrtabIndex].ByteSize := len(self.FSectionNames.Text);
    end;

    // Every section's file place after the ELF header, in index order (NOBITS none); the
    // section headers after them. Returns the file's size
    hidden method DoLayFile(): int64;
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LAlign: int64;
    begin
      LAt := ADAM_ELF_HEADER_SIZE;
      for LI := 1 to self.FHeaderCount - 1 do
        if self.FHeaders[LI].HeaderType = SHT_NOBITS then
          skip;
        end;
        LAlign := self.FHeaders[LI].Align;
        if LAlign > 1 then
          LAt := AlignUp(LAt, LAlign);
        end;
        self.FHeaders[LI].FileAt := LAt;
        LAt := LAt + self.FHeaders[LI].ByteSize;
      end;
      self.FHeadersAt := AlignUp(LAt, ADAM_ELF_TABLE_ALIGN);
      return self.FHeadersAt + ADAM_ELF_SECTION_HEADER_SIZE * self.FHeaderCount;
    end;

    // The ELF header (extended numbering past SHN_LORESERVE: see the header)
    hidden method DoElfHeader();
    begin
      self.FBytes[0] := ELFMAG0;
      self.FBytes[1] := ELFMAG1;
      self.FBytes[2] := ELFMAG2;
      self.FBytes[3] := ELFMAG3;
      self.FBytes[EI_CLASS] := ELFCLASS64;
      self.FBytes[EI_DATA] := ELFDATA2LSB;
      self.FBytes[EI_VERSION] := uint8(EV_CURRENT);
      self.FBytes[EI_OSABI] := ELFOSABI_SYSV;
      self.FBytes[EI_ABIVERSION] := 0;
      self.DoPut(16, uint64(ET_REL), 2);
      self.DoPut(18, uint64(self.FMachine.Machine), 2);
      self.DoPut(20, uint64(EV_CURRENT), 4);
      // no entry, no program headers, no flags
      self.DoPut(40, uint64(self.FHeadersAt), 8);
      self.DoPut(52, uint64(ADAM_ELF_HEADER_SIZE), 2);
      self.DoPut(58, uint64(ADAM_ELF_SECTION_HEADER_SIZE), 2);
      if self.FHeaderCount >= int64(SHN_LORESERVE) then
        self.DoPut(60, 0, 2);
        self.FHeaders[0].ByteSize := self.FHeaderCount;
      else
        self.DoPut(60, uint64(self.FHeaderCount), 2);
      end;
      if self.FShstrtabIndex >= int64(SHN_LORESERVE) then
        self.DoPut(62, uint64(SHN_XINDEX), 2);
        self.FHeaders[0].Link := self.FShstrtabIndex;
      else
        self.DoPut(62, uint64(self.FShstrtabIndex), 2);
      end;
    end;

    // The section header table
    hidden method DoSectionHeaders();
    var
      LI: int64;
      LAt: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to self.FHeaderCount - 1 do
        LAt := self.FHeadersAt + ADAM_ELF_SECTION_HEADER_SIZE * LI;
        self.DoPut(LAt, uint64(self.FHeaders[LI].NameAt), 4);
        self.DoPut(LAt + 4, uint64(self.FHeaders[LI].HeaderType), 4);
        self.DoPut(LAt + 8, self.FHeaders[LI].Flags, 8);
        // sh_addr 0 in an object
        self.DoPut(LAt + 24, uint64(self.FHeaders[LI].FileAt), 8);
        self.DoPut(LAt + 32, uint64(self.FHeaders[LI].ByteSize), 8);
        self.DoPut(LAt + 40, uint64(self.FHeaders[LI].Link), 4);
        self.DoPut(LAt + 44, uint64(self.FHeaders[LI].Info), 4);
        self.DoPut(LAt + 48, uint64(self.FHeaders[LI].Align), 8);
        self.DoPut(LAt + 56, uint64(self.FHeaders[LI].EntrySize), 8);
      end;
    end;

    // The relocation AReloc of ASection as its ELF type, symbol index and addend (see the
    // header); raises for one ELF cannot write or a field that is not zero
    hidden const method DoRelocOf(const ASection: ref Section; const AReloc: ref SectionReloc;
      var AType: int64; var ASymbol: int64; var AAddend: int64);
    var
      LSymbol: ref SectionSymbol;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      for LI := 0 to RelocWidth(AReloc.Kind) - 1 do
        if ASection.Bytes[AReloc.Offset + LI] <> 0 then
          raise(ADAM_ELF_FAULT_FIELD + ASection.SectionName + " " + HexText(AReloc.Offset));
        end;
      end;
      LSymbol := self.FSet.SymbolAt(AReloc.Symbol);
      ASymbol := self.FSymbolIndex[AReloc.Symbol];
      AAddend := AReloc.Addend;
      match AReloc.Kind of
        RelocKind.Rel32:
          // the field's own end is what Rel32 counts from
          AAddend := AReloc.Addend - 4;
          if LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Import then
            AType := self.FMachine.RelocGotPcRel;
          else
            if self.FMachine.IsCallField(ASection, AReloc.Offset) then
              AType := self.FMachine.RelocPlt32;
            else
              AType := self.FMachine.RelocPc32;
            end;
          end;
        RelocKind.Rva32: AType := self.FMachine.RelocPc32;
        RelocKind.Abs64:
          if LSymbol.Kind = SymbolKind.Import then
            raise(ADAM_ELF_FAULT_RELOC + "an Abs64 of the import " + LSymbol.SymbolName +
              " in " + ASection.SectionName);
          end;
          AType := self.FMachine.RelocAbs64;
        RelocKind.SecRel32: AType := self.FMachine.RelocDtpOff32;
        RelocKind.TpOff32: AType := self.FMachine.RelocTpOff32;
      else
        raise(ADAM_ELF_FAULT_RELOC + RelocKindText(AReloc.Kind) + " in " + ASection.SectionName);
      end;
    end;

    // The set section AId's bytes and its .rela entries
    hidden method DoSectionBody(const AId: int64);
    var
      LSection: ref Section;
      LReloc: ref SectionReloc;
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LType: int64;
      LSymbol: int64;
      LAddend: int64;
    begin
      LSection := self.FSet.SectionAt(AId);
      if LSection.Kind <> SectionKind.Zeroed then
        LAt := self.FHeaders[self.FSectionIndex[AId]].FileAt;
        for LI := 0 to LSection.Size() - 1 do
          self.FBytes[LAt + LI] := LSection.Bytes[LI];
        end;
      end;
      if self.FRelaIndex[AId] = 0 then
        return;
      end;
      LAt := self.FHeaders[self.FRelaIndex[AId]].FileAt;
      for LI := 0 to LSection.RelocCount - 1 do
        LReloc := LSection.RelocAt(LI);
        self.DoRelocOf(LSection, LReloc, LType, LSymbol, LAddend);
        self.DoPut(LAt, uint64(LReloc.Offset), 8);
        self.DoPut(LAt + 8, (uint64(LSymbol) shl 32) | uint64(LType), 8);
        self.DoPut(LAt + 16, uint64(LAddend), 8);
        LAt := LAt + ADAM_ELF_RELA_SIZE;
      end;
    end;

    // The Shared section AId's group: GRP_COMDAT, then its members' indices
    hidden method DoGroupBody(const AId: int64);
    var
      LWords: Int64Array;
      LAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
    begin
      LAt := self.FHeaders[self.FGroupIndex[AId]].FileAt;
      self.DoPut(LAt, uint64(GRP_COMDAT), 4);
      LWords := self.DoGroupWords(AId);
      for LI := 0 to len(LWords) - 1 do
        self.DoPut(LAt + ADAM_ELF_WORD_SIZE * (LI + 1), uint64(LWords[LI]), 4);
      end;
    end;

    // .symtab (and .symtab_shndx past the reserve), .strtab, .shstrtab
    hidden method DoTables();
    var
      LAt: int64;
      LShndxAt: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LIndex: int64;
      LText: string;
    begin
      LAt := self.FHeaders[self.FSymtabIndex].FileAt;
      LShndxAt := 0;
      if self.FShndxIndex <> 0 then
        LShndxAt := self.FHeaders[self.FShndxIndex].FileAt;
      end;
      for LI := 0 to self.FSymbolCount - 1 do
        LIndex := self.FSymbols[LI].SectionIndex;
        self.DoPut(LAt, uint64(self.FSymbols[LI].NameAt), 4);
        self.FBytes[LAt + 4] := self.FSymbols[LI].SymbolInfo;
        // st_other: STV_DEFAULT
        self.FBytes[LAt + 5] := STV_DEFAULT;
        if LIndex >= int64(SHN_LORESERVE) then
          self.DoPut(LAt + 6, uint64(SHN_XINDEX), 2);
          self.DoPut(LShndxAt + ADAM_ELF_WORD_SIZE * LI, uint64(LIndex), 4);
        else
          self.DoPut(LAt + 6, uint64(LIndex), 2);
        end;
        self.DoPut(LAt + 8, uint64(self.FSymbols[LI].SymbolValue), 8);
        // st_size 0: a SectionSet keeps no symbol's size
        LAt := LAt + ADAM_ELF_SYMBOL_SIZE;
      end;
      LText := self.FStrings.Text;
      LAt := self.FHeaders[self.FStrtabIndex].FileAt;
      for LI := 0 to len(LText) - 1 do
        self.FBytes[LAt + LI] := uint8(LText[LI]);
      end;
      LText := self.FSectionNames.Text;
      LAt := self.FHeaders[self.FShstrtabIndex].FileAt;
      for LI := 0 to len(LText) - 1 do
        self.FBytes[LAt + LI] := uint8(LText[LI]);
      end;
    end;

    // The object's bytes (see the header)
    method Run(): ByteArray;
    var
      LTotal: int64;
      LI: int64;
      LId: int64;
    begin
      self.DoCheckSections();
      self.DoNumberSections();
      self.DoMarkThreadSymbols();
      self.DoNumberSymbols();
      self.DoDescribeSections();
      LTotal := self.DoLayFile();
      // Every byte no field writes (padding, unused fields) is zero
      setlength(self.FBytes, LTotal);
      for LI := 0 to LTotal - 1 do
        self.FBytes[LI] := 0;
      end;
      self.DoElfHeader();
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        if self.FSet.SectionAt(LId).Shared then
          self.DoGroupBody(LId);
        end;
      end;
      for LId := 1 to self.FSet.SectionCount - 1 do
        self.DoSectionBody(LId);
      end;
      self.DoTables();
      self.DoSectionHeaders();
      return self.FBytes;
    end;
  end;

// ASections as one ELF64 relocatable object for the arch AMachine describes (see the
// header); raises for a nil input and for what the object cannot hold
public routine WriteElfObject(const ASections: ref SectionSet;
  const AMachine: ref ElfMachine): ByteArray;
var
  LWriter: ref ElfWriter;
begin
  if (ASections = nil) or (AMachine = nil) then
    raise(ADAM_ELF_FAULT_NO_INPUT);
  end;
  LWriter := ref ElfWriter(ASections, AMachine);
  return LWriter.Run();
end;

end.
